    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="1086" n="991" xml:id="pg991"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3394/235: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-11T16:00:00-04:00">August 11, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>225. Send following message to American Embassy at Tokyo by telegraph: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Inquire of appropriate authorities whether following proposed visits of
                            the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Gold Star</hi> are agreeable to
                            Japanese Government: Truk, September 10 to September 12; Palau,
                            September 17 to September 19; Miike, October 12 to October 14; Yokohama,
                            October 18 to October 23; Saipan, October 29 to October 31.<anchor
                                n="62" xml:id="d929-f1"/> Inform Department by telegraph of reply of
                            Japanese authorities.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d929-f1" n="62" xml:id="d929-f1-content">
                <p>Truk, Palau, and Saipan were located in the Japanese Mandate.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
